  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/assets/5f770f5be6b6131533dc23482281e82024737a4e5a61440dfe1baf5108786381.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $y=g(x)$ is shown above. \nApproximate ${g}^{\u2032}(x)$ at the point $x=6$ using a forward difference approximation with step size $h=4.$",
  "worked_solution": "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{g}^{\u2032}(x)\u2248\\frac{g(x+h)-g(x)}{h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=6.$  Applying the above formula with $x=6$ and $h=4$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{\u2032}(6) & \u2248\\frac{g(6+4)-g(6)}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(10)-g(6)}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{8-2}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{4} \\\\  & =1.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
